+---
+title: Testing click.utils to full line+branch coverage
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 2, tokens: 61977 }
+touches:
+  - tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py
+  - src/click/utils.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- Extra click.utils tests live in tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py; with the rest of the suite they reach 100% line+branch coverage of src/click/utils.py.
+- Platform branches of get_app_dir are tested by monkeypatching `click.utils.WIN` and `sys.platform`, not by skipping per OS.
+- Fake stdout for `-` handling (_LazyFile, open_file, _get_*_stream) is `io.TextIOWrapper(io.BytesIO())` monkeypatched onto sys.stdout, so pytest's capture is never touched.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- Bad glob patterns (e.g. "[bad", "test.py::x") do not raise re.error on Python 3.14, so the `except re.error` in _expand_args is reached only by monkeypatching `glob.glob` (it is imported inside the function, so patching the module attribute works).
+- A custom writer object can't reach echo's "bytes but no binary writer" branch: _is_binary_writer probes with write(b"") and accepts it. Only a real text-only stream (StringIO) gets there, and then echo raises TypeError.
+
+## Watch out
+- pytest runs with filterwarnings=error: the deprecated click.utils aliases (LazyFile, safecall, get_text_stream, ...) must be accessed inside pytest.warns(DeprecationWarning).
+- make_str uses sys.getfilesystemencoding() (utf-8 on macOS/Linux); use invalid UTF-8 like b"\xff" to hit the replace fallback.
+- mypy/pyright only check src and tests/typing, so editor type warnings about mock objects in tests/test_utils are not CI failures.
